### Security and Best Practices 
1. Additional security measures - Use HTTPS for secure communication. - Implement JWT or OAuth for authentication. - Add rate limiting to prevent abuse. 
2. Input validation and sanitization - Use libraries like express-validator or Joi to validate and sanitize inputs. - Prevent injection attacks by escaping user input. 
3. API versioning and backward compatibility - Use URL versioning (e.g., /v1/books) or headers. - Maintain backward compatibility by avoiding breaking changes or providing migration paths.
